hese challenges. However, their attack focuses on recovering as much data as possible, and therefore the fidelity of individual recovered sequences degrades as the number of sequences increases. On the\nother hand, attackers often only care about the few sequences that contain privacy-critical information, and are happy to forego fidelity of irrelevant sequences in exchange for accurate recovery of valuable sequences. Based on this philosophy, we propose a novel attacking algorithm that filters out irrelevant mixed embedding, enabling an attacker to pan for privacy-relevant sequences even out of extremely large-scale aggregation."
